cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MutaXplorer, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "MutaXplorer: comprehensive variant analysis for WGS, WES and targeted panels"
abstract: >-
  MutaXplorer is an open-source Nextflow pipeline for integrated DNA and RNA variant
  analysis of whole-genome, whole-exome and targeted-panel sequencing. It accepts DNA
  FASTQ or BAM (including DRAGEN / Illumina Connected Analytics output) and RNA FASTQ on
  hg19 or hg38, and performs somatic (tumour-only or tumour-normal) and germline SNV/indel
  calling (GATK Mutect2, HaplotypeCaller), copy-number analysis (CNVkit), structural-variant
  calling (Manta), DNA and RNA fusion detection (Manta, STAR + Arriba), tumour mutational
  burden, microsatellite instability (MSIsensor2), mutational signatures and sample-identity
  checks. Results are annotated with Ensembl VEP and combined in cohort tables, an Excel
  workbook and an interactive HTML report. Includes a simulated test suite and benchmark.
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-28
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/deppworld/mutaxplorer"
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - variant calling
  - somatic mutations
  - germline variants
  - copy number
  - structural variants
  - gene fusions
  - tumour mutational burden
  - microsatellite instability
  - Nextflow
